trategic alliance between two powerful noble families in the region."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1251, "end": 1266, "text": "As noted by Dr."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1267, "end": 1442, "text": "Oehler, \"The union strengthened the position of both the House of Henneberg and the House of Wettin, to which Frederick III belonged, in the complex web of medieval politics.\""}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1443, "end": 1578, "text": "In terms of their reign, Catherine and Frederick III worked together to consolidate their power and influence in Thuringia and Meissen."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1579, "end": 1761, "text": "During their joint rule, they implemented several key reforms, including the establishment of a more centralized administration and the promotion of trade and commerce in the region."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1762, "end": 1986, "text": "While the exact dates of their marriage and reign are not universally agreed upon, the overwhelming majority of historical sources confirm that Catherine of Henneberg and Frederick III were indeed married and ruled together."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1987, "end": 2194, "text": "In conclusion, the evidence from medieval records and expert testimony leaves no doubt that Catherine of Henneberg was married to Frederick III, solidifying their place in the annals of German noble history."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2195, "end": 2206, "text": "References:"}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2208, "end": 2270, "text": "(1) Johannes Rothe, \"Thuringian Chronicle,\" late 14th century."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2271, "end": 2303, "text": "(2) \"Meissen Urkundenbuch,\" Vol."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Catherine 